---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'

const branches = [
  { number: '01', name: 'NLSM', role: 'rank-jump associated grade', formula: 'gr_R(Scalar cells) → regional Catalan transfer → QTDS', status: 'all-core coefficients exact · chain assembly open' },
  { number: '02', name: 'Yang–Mills', role: 'first normal jet', formula: 'H_gauge(J¹ Scalar)', status: 'working structure' },
  { number: '03', name: 'Gravity', role: 'primitive symmetric retract', formula: 'PrimSym²_g(J¹ Scalar)', status: 'tree + cuts' },
]
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Marici · Scalar master geometry"
  description="A research map for intrinsic theory-producing operations and the cyclic/BV lifting problem."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Scalar master geometry · research ledger</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">One geometry.<br /><em>Several theories.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Marici studies whether normal layers, boundary operations, pairings, and sewing structures of a scalar surface intrinsically produce NLSM, Yang–Mills, and gravity.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="primary-action" href="#frontier">Open the active frontier</a>
        <a class="text-action" href="/ledger/">Read the published ledger</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="coordinate-card" aria-label="Current research coordinates">
      <p class="coordinate-kicker">Current bounded projection</p>
      <dl class="metric-grid">
        <div><dt>Branches</dt><dd>3</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tree selector</dt><dd>✓</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Cut sewing</dt><dd>✓</dd></div>
        <div><dt>BV lift</dt><dd>?</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="coordinate-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span><i></i><b>J¹</b></span><span><i></i><b>Pₑ</b></span><span><i></i><b>Mod</b></span></div>
      <p class="coordinate-note">Closure on cuts does not by itself select an off-shell integrand representative.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="authority-strip" aria-label="Epistemic status">
    <div><span class="status-light"></span><p><strong>Established</strong><br />Tree pairing and pure-state selector</p></div>
    <div><span class="strip-index">∞</span><p><strong>Generalized cuts</strong><br />Closed under induced Einstein sewing</p></div>
    <div><span class="strip-index">01</span><p><strong>Open obstruction</strong><br />Canonical chain-level trace lift</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="branches" aria-labelledby="branches-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Theory-producing operations</p><h2 id="branches-title">Three distinct mechanisms</h2></div>
      <p>Rank jump, normal jet, and primitive symmetric sewing are kept distinct rather than collapsed into a single double-copy slogan.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="dimension-grid">
      {branches.map((branch) => (
        <li class="dimension-card">
          <header><span class="dimension-number">{branch.number}</span><div><p class="dimension-role">{branch.role}</p><h3>{branch.name}</h3></div></header>
          <code class="formula">{branch.formula}</code>
          <span class="status-pill">{branch.status}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="frontier-section" id="frontier" aria-labelledby="frontier-title">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Active Nima theorem target</p><h2 id="frontier-title">Assemble the regional transfer into one chain map</h2></div>
        <p>The direct Catalan bijection and the directed-forest sink rule now identify every partial-core scalar sector with QTDS at all even arity. What remains is compatibility between different core strata before coefficient augmentation.</p>
      </div>
      <article class="frontier-card frontier-card--gap">
        <header><p>Core-incidence / worldsheet assembly</p><span>open</span></header>
        <h3>⊗<sub>R</sub> Φ<sub>R</sub> &nbsp; ⇝ &nbsp; Φ<sub>cell</sub> &nbsp; ⇝ &nbsp; Φ<sub>Poch/Cousin</sub></h3>
        <p>Construct the higher homotopies relating regional Catalan maps when a physical core edge is added or removed. The resulting deck-equivariant cellular map must preserve cuts and then lift through the filtered Pochhammer/Cousin comparison to the worldsheet half-class.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="snapshot-callout" id="ledger" aria-labelledby="ledger-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Human-readable memory</p>
    <h2 id="ledger-title">The ledger records claims with their perimeter.</h2>
    <p>Entries live in <code>src/ledger</code> and explicitly distinguish established structure, strong inference, open questions, and prohibited overclaims.</p>
    <a class="text-action" href="/ledger/">Open the published ledger →</a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
